 "inference": [
  "Both tanks, both IFVs, the Gepard, the JLTV and the Marauder store delay 12 s and a rate of exactly 10 percent of root health per second: EA's new values. The rate is in health per second, so a tank regains 120 per second and an armoured transport 80.",
  "The AAV7A1 stores 6 s and 5 percent: EA's values from before 1.3.1.0.",
  "Aircraft are not in EA's statement: helicopters and jets store 17.5 s and 10 percent. Light vehicles and boats store 12 s and 10 percent, dirt bikes 10 s and 10 percent, stationary weapons 5 or 10 s and 5 percent, the MQ-9 and the Beast no regeneration.",
  "The registry rows Passives_Vehicles_MBT_Regeneration (delay 9.5, rate 132) and IFV (9.5, 110) are 110 percent of the base rate with a shorter delay. EA says the Vehicle Regeneration passive was replaced by Mine Sweeping in 1.3.1.0, so these rows may be unused.",
  "EA's 80 percent slowdown at critical health was not found as a stored number in the root object."
 ],
